  "reason": "Monty rejects class inheritance at parse time. The pinned Monty v1.0.0 documentation (commit 85c5d1f6bef038405cfc40a4eed94806e303567e) lists base classes / metaclasses as a parse-time rejection, raising NotImplementedError before any code runs. A BrassClaw PythonCode component runs inside that same Monty execution context, so it cannot inherit from a Python base class. Use simple classes (instance methods, __init__, class variables) instead, which are supported. This is a language limitation, not a BrassClaw authoring restriction.",
